From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:29:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Implement FillMesh().

FillMesh() recorded into command lists and otherwise did nothing.  Measured on Windows
(build 29671), a mesh is its triangles drawn one after another: where two overlap the
brush blends twice, an edge two share is drawn once by the top-left rule, either winding
is drawn and a degenerate triangle is not; the world transform applies.  A target that is
not aliased, or a mesh that was never closed, is D2DERR_WRONG_STATE, and an empty mesh
draws nothing.  The triangles are already a vertex buffer, three points each.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ee62e2839b90b8cc9485404110b4467fc875d988)

